       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify that a protocol exists, and 1600 mg four times daily (6400 mg/day) is double the maximum daily dose of 3200 mg. A 1600 mg single dose is also twice the usual 800 mg per-dose limit. I don't know of any standard protocol that supports this, and the harms it risks (GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events) can be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3200 mg/day), or 600 mg by mouth every 6 hours. I'll enter either right away if you tell me which.\n- **Route the high-dose order through your pharmacy's override process.** If a protocol really does exist, the pharmacist or prescriber who reviewed it can place or authorize the order through your hospital's formal exception pathway. That process can check the protocol, the monitoring plan, and any documented rationale in a way I can't.\n\nLet me know if you'd like me to enter one of the in-range options."
